{"availability":"available","full":"rsasaki0109/CloudAnalyzer","name":"CloudAnalyzer","description":"Browser-based LiDAR tools for SLAM map correction, point-cloud analysis, and editable Lanelet2 vector-map drafting. Runs locally with Rust + WebAssembly.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":17,"forks":3,"created":"2026-03-18T01:59:07Z","updated":"2026-10-04T06:49:39Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://rsasaki0109.github.io/CloudAnalyzer/","topics":["autoware","change-detection","lanelet2","las","lidar","point-cloud","python","rust","slam","surveying","threejs","vector-map","webassembly"],"demo":"https://rsasaki0109.github.io/CloudAnalyzer/app/?demo=nclt-seasons","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T05:50:31.948Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T05:50:31.948Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T05:50:31.948Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T06:50:50.538Z","stars":17,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-05T05:50:31.948Z","stars":17,"forks":3}],"technologies":["Three.js","Python","Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Fix your SLAM map, clean it, measure it. In the browser.","CloudAnalyzer is a point cloud viewer and analyzer that runs in your browser: open a ROS bag or a drive's poses and scans, close its loops, take out the cars that drove past, and compare the result with last month's map or the ground truth. Everything runs locally in Rust compiled to WebAssembly, on every core: nothing to install, and your data never leaves your machine.","A loop closed by hand on a real drive (NCLT, University of Michigan): the same place seen twice a kilometre apart, lined up with ICP, and the drive pulled together"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rsasaki0109/CloudAnalyzer/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"be86a548281db4bb2a117850298559da5e122400a5fbff633f815e0653c1159f","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T06:50:50.631Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:50:50.631Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDo